course: dictionary
lesson: 15020
title: Respiration: breathing and energy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Respiration has two meanings. The everyday meaning is breathing: taking air into the lungs and letting it out. «Breathing in fresh air filled my lungs» is about this meaning.
explain: In science, respiration is a process that happens in every living cell. It uses oxygen and food (glucose) to release energy, and it gives off carbon dioxide and water. «Plants respire day and night» means their cells are doing this all the time, even in the dark.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is meant. If the sentence talks about lungs and air, it means breathing. If it talks about cells, energy or glucose, it means the science process. «The first aider gave artificial respiration» means rescue breaths, given to someone who has stopped breathing.
fact: Respiration is an uncountable noun, so we say «some respiration», not «a respiration».
fact: Breathing moves air in and out of the lungs; respiration happens inside every living cell to release energy.
fact: Respiration uses oxygen and food (glucose) and gives off carbon dioxide and water.
fact: «Aerobic respiration» means respiration that uses oxygen.
fact: «Rate of respiration» means how fast the process of respiration is happening.
exercise: «Breathing moves air, but respiration happens inside every cell.» What is the main difference? | Breathing makes food for the body | Respiration only happens in the lungs | Breathing and respiration are exactly the same | *Respiration releases energy inside cells
exercise: «The first aider gave artificial respiration to the man who had stopped breathing.» Who was artificial respiration for? | A runner who was tired | *Someone who had stopped breathing | A car with a flat tyre | A plant in the sunshine
exercise: Which is the everyday meaning of respiration? | Turning food into a new living cell | *Taking air into the lungs and letting it out | Using oxygen and food to make a plant grow | Giving off light in the dark
test: «Plants respire day and night, even in the dark.» What does respire mean here? | Make a loud noise | Drink water only | Turn green in the sunlight | *Use oxygen and food to release energy
test: What does «rate of respiration» mean? | How far a living thing can run | The amount of water in the air | The number of breaths in a lung | *How fast the process of respiration is happening
exam: Which statement about respiration is true? | Breathing and respiration are exactly the same thing | Respiration only happens in the lungs | *Respiration happens in every living cell, releasing energy | Respiration makes food for the plant
